==========================================================================
  APPENDIX I -- PRODUCTION FROM THE BOUNDARY
  the boundaries produce the standing addresses; nothing is formed
  and discarded, and the envelope is never traversed
==========================================================================

I.1  THE THREE CONDITIONS OF A BOUNDARY
     classify() against an independent condition, computed by
     inspecting the support one content at a time.  Exhaustive over
     every boundary and every partial orientation of its support.

    PASS  Instance 1: condition correct on every partial orientation   2752/2752
    PASS  Instance 2: condition correct on every partial orientation   3264/3264

I.2  FORCING IS SOUND
     when a boundary forces an orientation, the opposite orientation
     places the descent inside that boundary's excluded sector.
     Verified on every forcing condition that can arise.

    PASS  Instance 1: forcing dictates the only admissible orientation   129/129
    PASS  Instance 2: forcing dictates the only admissible orientation   153/153

I.3  FORCING IS COMPLETE -- THE EXCLUDED SECTOR IS UNREACHABLE
     a sector becomes reachable only at its last unoriented content,
     and forcing orients that content one step earlier.  Tested by
     requiring that no boundary is ever MATCHED at a descent that
     applied forcing to exhaustion.

    PASS  Instance 1: no produced address lies in any excluded sector   [15 produced, 0 inside a sector]
    PASS  Instance 2: no produced address lies in any excluded sector   [10 produced, 0 inside a sector]

